  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe proposed solution addresses the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by employing a continuous optimization approach that leverages the self-overlap properties of the function h(x). The core idea is to\n- Find a step function minimizing the maximum overlap with its shifted complement\n- Represent the function as a normalized histogram with fixed integral\n- Balance magnitude and placement of the function values to avoid repeated regions\nThe approach differs from previous strategies by:\n1. Using analytic projection methods\n2. Applying coordinate descent to Lagrangian multipliers\n3. Implementing an adaptive refinement scheme\n4. Maintaining theoretical guarantees through dual formulations\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nVariables: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f\u207a with \u2211h_i = n/2 (where n=70)\nObjective: minimize C5 = dx \u00b7 max\u2096 (np.correlate(h,1-h,'full')).max()\nConstraints: 0 \u2264 h\u1d62 \u2264 1\u2200i\nSubproblem formulation:\n  minimize\u209c max\u1d62[{h_i(1-h_{i+k})+\u03bb|i-k|+\u03bc|i-k|}]\n  subject to \u2211h\u1d62=35\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\na) Initialization\n  Store_parent(parent_h): repair initial solution using iterative clipping\n  Parametrize(dx=2/n)\n  Initial population: {repair(np.random.rand(n)) for n_perturbations}\nb) Optimization cycle:\n  While time < budget:\n    Sample candidates via analytic projection using:\n      h\u1d62 = projection_operator(random_shift, window_width)\n    Repair integral constraint using:\n      h_adjust = clip_and_scale(sum(h_goal))\n    Evaluate objective using finite correlation\n    Select top candidates (lowest C5)\n    Refine winners with gradient descent (100 steps)\n    C5(t) = median filter of evaluations\n    Break rigorously if convergence detected\nc) Repair function:\n  def _repair(h,n): clip, then adjust sum by interpolation\n\n4. Search Choices\n- Initial population: 100 variants with step sizes [0.05,0.15]\n- Projection weights: kernel function K(|dx|) = exp(-\u03b1|x|\u00b2)\n- Adaptivity: window_width = 7-region windows\n- C5_trend: minimum improvement period 2000 evaluations\n\n5. Computebudget and robustness\nLoop time: \u2248 (n\u00b736\u00b7standard_deviation)\u4f46\u6211\u9700\u8981\u7ee7\u7eed\u5199\u5b8c\u6574\u7b56\u7565",
